B. Northlight OS terms (part 2: the author's own work)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

You may, without asking:
  - read the source code and learn from it;
  - build it for yourself and install it on your own TVs;
  - share links to this repository and its official releases.

You must ask the author first, and have written permission, before you:
  - change the source code and share, publish or distribute the changed version;
  - redistribute the source code or the APKs anywhere other than this repository;
  - use the Northlight OS name, logo or artwork for another project or product;
  - use any of this work commercially (selling it, bundling it with devices, or in paid services).

How to ask: open an issue on the official Northlight OS GitHub repository, say what you want to change or
share and why, and wait for the author's written reply there. Permission given for one request does not
cover others.

Suggestions and fixes are welcome: open an issue or a pull request. By sending a pull request you agree
that the author may use your change in Northlight OS under these terms.

Part 1 above remains under the MIT License; these terms do not take away any right that licence gives
for cleanyourtv's own code. Where a file contains both MIT-licensed code and Northlight OS changes, the MIT notice applies to
the MIT parts and these terms apply to the rest.

